{
  "title": "Consolidate duplicated website timeline processing",
  "description": "The game viewer, golden viewer helpers, and prerender \
pipeline maintain separate implementations of timeline behavior. \
mergeLlmEvents exists in game-log-helpers.ts, game-viewer.js, and \
prerender-timeline.ts; the prerender copy already differs by tracking \
maxGameSeq. Turn counting, phase labels, event rendering, and entity decoding \
also have overlapping implementations. This makes browser, golden, and \
prerendered views vulnerable to behavioral drift. Move pure event merging, \
ordering, turn/phase calculation, and safe text decoding into a shared typed \
module, leaving DOM construction in the consumers. Replace game-viewer.js's \
detached innerHTML entity decoder with decodeHtmlEntitiesOnce. Add parity \
tests that run representative events through prerender, replay, and golden \
consumers and assert identical ordering and visibility boundaries.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "website",
    "cleanup",
    "testing",
  ],
